re is a "rule of thumb": TPSA < 60-70 for good BBB penetration. This molecule\'s TPSA is 72.55, which is borderline.\\n\\nWe could also compute the logD at pH 7.4 (estimate_logd) to see if the molecule is ionized at physiological pH. The carbamate group (urethane) is not ionizable (amide-like). The hydroxyl group is not ionizable. So the molecule is neutral at pH 7.4. That\'s good for passive diffusion.\\n\\nLet\'s compute logD.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "estimate_logd", "parameters": {"smiles": "CCC(O)(COC(N)=O)c1ccccc1"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "Estimated logD at pH 7.4: 1.3795\\nlogP (Wildman-Crippen): 1.3795\\nFraction neutral at pH 7.4: 1.0000\\nNumber of basic sites: 1\\nNumber of acidic sites: 3\\nMost basic pKa: 2.8062\\nMost acidic pKa: 13.0856\\nMapped SMILES: [C:1]([C:2]([C:3]([O:4][H:21])([C:5]([O:6][C:7]([N:8]([H:24])[H:25])=[O:9])([H:22])[H:23])[c:10]1[c:11]([H:26])[c:12]([H:27])[c:13]([H:28])[c:14]([H:29])[c:15]1[H:30])([H:19])[H:20])([H:16])([H:17])[H:18]\\nWarnings: Multiple acidic sites; using only most_acidic_pka for neutral-fraction estimate.; Amphoteric molecule; neutral-fraction estimate assumes independent sites.", "function_name": "estimate_logd", "arguments": {"smiles": "CCC(O)(COC(N)=O)c1ccccc1"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nInteresting: the prediction says there are 1 basic site and 3 acidic sites. However, the molecule likely has no basic or acidic sites. The pKa values: most basic pKa = 2.8062 (maybe the hydroxyl group? pKa of alcohols is around 16-18, not basic). Actually, the carbamate NH2 might have a pKa around 9-10? But the prediction says acidic sites with pKa 13.0856 (maybe the carbamate NH2 is acidic? Not typical). This might be a misassignment. But anyway, the molecule is neutral at pH 7.4 (fraction neutral = 1.0). So logD ≈ logP = 1.38.\\n\\nNow, let\'s check for any structural alerts that might cause poor BBB penetration. Use score_structural_alerts. This might id